        "title": "Logic and Computability: Undecidability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Computability theory and mathematical logic are the same subject viewed from two angles.\nThe undecidability of FOL validity (Church-Turing 1936) and the incompleteness of PA\n(Gödel 1931) are two facets of the same phenomenon: the halting problem. The arithmetic\nhierarchy stratifies the degrees of undecidability."
